ists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahamCampbell/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahamCampbell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahamCampbell/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahamCampbell/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahamCampbell/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahamCampbell/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahamCampbell/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/laravel/framework/issues/comments/58764987","html_url":"https://github.com/laravel/framework/issues/5997#issuecomment-58764987","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/laravel/framework/issues/5997","id":58764987,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU4NzY0OTg3","user":{"login":"thers","id":213272,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzI3Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/213272?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers","html_url":"https://github.com/thers","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2014-10-11T21:23:20Z","updated_at":"2014-10-11T21:34:03Z","body":"After a research i found that the problem place isn't scanner itslef, but the test, `Scanner::getRouteDefinitions()` returns normal code that works perfect. Problem is with whitespaces. As we all know on Windows newline is formed by two special characters `\\r\\n` but on *nix it is only `\\n`.\nSo test could be fixed like that:\n\n``` php\n<?php\n\nuse Illuminate\\Routing\\Annotations\\Scanner;\n\nclass RoutingAnnotationScannerTest extends PHPUnit_Framework_TestCase {\n\n    public function testProperRouteDefinitionsAreGenerated()\n    {\n        require_once __DIR__.'/fixtures/annotations/BasicController.php';\n        $scanner = Scanner::create(__DIR__.'/fixtures/annotations', 'App\\Http\\Controllers');\n\n        $replace_pairs = [\n            \"\\n\" => \"\",\n            \"\\r\" => \"\"\n        ];\n\n        $actual = strtr($scanner->getRouteDefinitions(), $replace_pairs);\n        $expected = strtr(trim(file_get_contents(__DIR__.'/results/annotation-basic.php')), $replace_pairs);\n\n        $this->assertEquals($expected, $actual);\n    }\n\n}\n\n```\n\nNot sure that this is a good proof, I'll just leave it here http://take.ms/lJvS6 :)\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/laravel/framework/issues/comments/58764987/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"thers","id":213272,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzI3Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/213272?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers","html_url":"https://github.com/thers","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thers/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/u